# Every part stands alone

**Wadhu** (by Gotigin, *Tools · Apps · More*) holds reusable code: crates, apps and tools that other Gotigin brands' apps (e.g. Kumkaj) need and that anyone else can use. Canonical text: `docs/WADHU_VISION_AND_PRINCIPLES.md` §1–5; crate rules: `docs/CRATES.md`.

## Do

- Put generic, brand-neutral libraries in `crates/<name>/` (package `wadhu-<name>`) and standalone programs in `apps/<name>/`.
- Let apps (and sites) depend on crates by path.
- When a crate has a core plus Makepad UI, put the UI behind an optional `widgets` feature **of the same crate**.
- Take Makepad as `makepad-widgets = { workspace = true }` (registry name + root `[patch.crates-io]`).
- Give each app its own `env/`, `scripts/`, `docs/` and `tools/<app>-dev` shim; root `scripts/` name no app.
- Version each crate with SemVer and a `CHANGELOG.md`; add behaviour as new API or options with the old default.
- Create parts with `./scripts/new-app.sh` / `./scripts/new-crate.sh`; run `./scripts/check-independence.sh` before finishing.

## Do not

- Make an app depend on a sibling app, or a crate depend on a sibling crate or on any app. If two parts need the same code, copy it (copy-then-diverge) or make it a crate an app uses.
- Point a crate at `vendor/` by path (it breaks consumers in other workspaces).
- Put any brand's product/business logic (books, KOT, AWB, …) in Wadhu. It stays in the product app that owns it.
- Depend on anything under `templates/`; copy it.
- Restate a root doc in an app/crate doc; link to it.

```text
✅ apps/print-bridge → crates/escpos            ✅ Kumkaj app → wadhu crates/escpos (+ one [patch] line)
❌ apps/print-bridge → apps/label-maker         ❌ crates/escpos-widgets → crates/escpos (use a feature)
```
